From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:57:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] yblod-50: resynchronise a Dolby Vision FEL after a
 pairing fault

A single fault in the enhancement-layer pairing (a packet without a
time, a parser miss, a missing enhancement picture, 16 base pictures
waiting) froze the video for good: GetPicture returned VC_ERROR on every
call until a seek, the base decoder was no longer drained, and nothing
said why.

dvbridge_fel now records why the pairing failed (dvbridge_fel_error).
The decoder logs the first fault of a title at WARNING with that reason,
restarts the pairing (it resynchronises at the next common key frame, as
after a seek) and meanwhile shows the base pictures with their metadata,
as a MEL plays. After DV_FEL_RESYNCS (3) restarts the enhancement layer
is not decoded until the next seek. At the end of the stream base
pictures left without a partner are shown instead of an error.

An enhancement-layer decoder that cannot be created no longer fails the
whole decoder: the title plays from the base layer and metadata.
